===Etymology===
From the South German diminutive {{term|Fensterl||small window|lang=de}}. See {{m|de|Fenster}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-at-fensterln.ogg|Audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{IPA|/ˈfɛnstɐln/|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|fensterlt|fensterlte|gefensterlt}}

# {{lb|de|southern Germany|Austrian|Switzerland}} to visit a [[girl]] who is the object of one's affections at night, either by coming to her [[window]] or by climbing through it into her room
#*'''1996''', Roland Girtler, ''Sommergetreide: vom Untergang der bäuerlichen Kultur'', p. 105:
#*:Die Alten waren zwar selber einmal jung und haben auch '''gefensterlt''', aber trotzdem haben sie gepaßt.
#*:The old men were indeed young once themselves and have visited girls at night, but nevertheless they have been suitable.{{attention|de|please check translation}}

